d, with no documented revert to the last-known-good plaintext user_data"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add to AC3b or the hazard section: 'Back-out: if the next-boot confirmation fails, re-apply the previous user_data render (git revert of the base64gzip change) which AC2 has already shown is an in-place update, and reboot.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"low","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","AC item 'AC1 [non-codebase] `terraform plan` GENERATES against `origin/main`: it exits 0 ' cites operational evidence (iac) that lives outside the codebase; tag it [non-codebase] — prefix the checkbox text with [non-codebase] so the completion verifier accepts a recorded attestation instead of failing to find code proof.","AC item \"AC5 The drift workflow branches on `terraform plan -detailed-exitcode`'s EXISTIN\" cites operational evidence (iac) that lives outside the codebase; tag it [non-codebase] — prefix the checkbox text with [non-codebase] so the completion verifier accepts a recorded attestation instead of failing to find code proof."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Cite a concrete source (AL2023 cloud-init version + its documented gzip/`1f 8b` user-data handling, or a documented AWS user_data gzip acceptance reference) for the assumption that cloud-init on this image decompresses a gzip user_data_base64 payload, rather than asserting it from general knowledge; classify the evidence (Verified vs Partially-verified) and, if it stays Unverified, name it as the residual risk the AC3b deferral covers.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.5425,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'cloud-init accepts gzipped user-data, and at 73% comments this file compresses very well' — asserted without citation","AC3b: 'What IS proven in-session is AC3a plus the `1f 8b` gzip magic cloud-init dispatches on' — the dispatch behavior itself is asserted, not verified","user_data.sh:3 targets 'AL2023, arm64/Graviton' — a specific distro/arch whose cloud-init version is the actual consumer of the gzip payload","This is the mechanism the whole ticket rests on: if cloud-init on this image does not accept gzip on the user_data_base64 path, the next boot silently executes no user_data (evidence class: Unverified)"],"finding":"The plan's central fix mechanism — clou